        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇮🇱 Israel - Double tap strike.</strong> Israel has intensified large-scale airstrikes across Lebanon, including Beirut and southern regions, killing more than a dozen people. One strike in the Ramlet al-Baida seafront area, killed eight people and injured 31. Additional attacks across southern Lebanon and towns near Beirut have raised the death toll from Israeli strikes since late February to more than 630 (<a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/12/israeli-double-tap-strike-hits-displaced-on-beirut-seafront-kills-eight" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">double trouble</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇮🇷 Iran - Conditions to end the war</strong>. Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has outlined Tehran’s conditions for ending the ongoing conflict. He stated that any resolution must recognize Iran’s rights, include reparations for damages, and provide firm international guarantees against future attacks. The proposal was shared publicly on social media and reiterated in calls with leaders of Russia and Pakistan as part of Iran’s diplomatic outreach (<a href="https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-sets-three-conditions-to-end-war-with-us-and-israel-demands-rights-recognition-and-reparations-13988544.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">rules of disengagement</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇪🇸 Spain - Hate speech tracker</strong>. PM Pedro Sánchez has announced a government-backed tool called “Hodio” designed to track and measure hate speech across major social media platforms. The system will analyze the presence, spread, and evolution of harmful content using academic criteria and publish reports every six months ranking platforms based on how effectively they address hate speech. The project will be managed by Spain’s Observatory of Racism and Xenophobia (<a href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260311-spain-to-deploy-tool-to-track-social-media-hate-speech" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">AI against speech</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇨🇱 Chile - President Sworn in</strong>. José Antonio Kast has been sworn in as Chile’s president, marking the country’s political shift to the right since the dictatorship of Augusto Pinochet. In his inaugural address, Kast pledged sweeping reforms to address what he called national “emergencies” in security, immigration, health, and employment. Kast also ordered government audits to assess the state of public institutions after the previous administration (<a href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260312-chile-marks-sharp-turn-to-the-right-as-new-hardline-president-vows-sweeping-reforms" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">take right</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
